Wi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T08:47:54Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T08:48:44Z","body":"I'm seeing a similar issue in 4.8. All windows pop up too big.\n\n<img width=\"2559\" height=\"1537\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d2bafa17-1ba5-47c1-bc0e-ad6b8e95801f\" />\n\nIt's like the scale is applied twice (#121006).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913015875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913221124","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113710#issuecomment-4913221124","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113710","id":4913221124,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJNnOBA","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T09:10:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T09:10:47Z","body":"@KoBeWi I can try replicating but first I need some more info. What environment and screen scale are you using? Does it \"grow\" every time the window opens, and lastly do you have libdecor installed or not?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913221124/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913298600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113710#issuecomment-4913298600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113710","id":4913298600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJNr8qA","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T09:20:02Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T09:20:02Z","body":"KDE Plasma with 145% scale. The window does not grow. libdecor is installed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913298600/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913788897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113710#issuecomment-4913788897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113710","id":4913788897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJOJ34Q","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T10:20:57Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T10:20:57Z","body":"Thanks kobewi, I managed to replicate the issue.\n\nI think it's a different bug: I can only replicate it when using the X11 backend, making and closing a window, then reopening on Wayland the same kind of window. This means that it's likely the save/restore feature getting confused between the two DSs way of working.\n\nI assume it's because of the whole absolute vs logical window size thing #113656 tried to work around. I'm not sure what would be the best way forward without straight up redoing window scale handling (which is planned I think?) or breaking something for regular users of either backend. Perhaps we could make the window save/restore data per DS instead of generic? It's kinda a bummer but window size does not seem like a universally compatible value right now, unfortunately. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913788897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913882923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113710#issuecomment-4913882923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113710","id":4913882923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJOPnKw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T10:33:02Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T10:33:47Z","body":"> I think it's a different bug: I can only replicate it when using the X11 backend, making and closing a window, then reopening on Wayland the same kind of window. This means that it's likely the save/restore feature getting confused between the two DSs way of working.\n\nThe Advanced Import dialog and EditorFileDialog don't remember their size. They always just appear big for me.\nCheck #121006, where removing the scale factor would fix the size (the FileDialog pops up with fixed size multipled by scale). What you are describing sounds like unrelated issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4913882923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4924626784","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113710#issuecomment-4924626784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113710","id":4924626784,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJYfXYA","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-09T11:35:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T11:35:06Z","body":"Right. I don't know why but it only sometimes triggers on my setup. That's another bug to be taken care of then but hopefully it's less severe xD\n\nIt's very fiddly to debug but my current theory is that it's not constraining for two reasons:\n\n 1. the output size is still in \"unscaled terms\" so Godot picks the wrong size in e.g. `popup_centered_ratio`\n 2. kde does not do the constraining because it reports a (currently unused) `configure_bounds` and trusts us to do the right thing, unlike sway.\n\nWe can't really fix the platform-agnostic logic as it would break other DSes (for now), so I'll try making it honor the preferred bounds and see if that makes the issue at least bearable.\n\nThat is, assuming that my theory is correct. I'll keep investigating.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4924626784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]